<title>ITALY: Intermobiliare to become bank from 1997.</title>
<headline>Intermobiliare to become bank from 1997.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's Intermobiliare, the only stockbroking and fund management company quoted on the Milan stock market, is to become a bank from January 1997.</p>
<p>The Turin-based company said it will change its name to Banca Intermobiliare di Investimenti e Gestioni (BIIG) with branches in Milan, Genoa, Pavia, Ivrea and Rome.</p>
<p>It obtained the Bank of Italy's authorisation to change its status last week.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
